      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Union County Courthouse, with its stonework, stands as a 19th‑century symbol of the town’s railroad‑era prosperity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://brainbound.blog/liberty-indiana-guide",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Liberty’s historic core, including the Courthouse Square Historic District, is listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://brainbound.blog/liberty-indiana-guide",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Whitewater Memorial State Park, just outside Liberty, offers hiking, water activities, and a glimpse of the region’s natural beauty.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://brainbound.blog/liberty-indiana-guide",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town hosts the Union County Public Library, a lending library that serves the community’s educational needs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
